  "notes": "Beyond the indirect object, the dative marks the person a statement is ABOUT: interest or disadvantage (mihi), purpose in the double-dative pattern (auxiliō nōbīs), and possession with sum (liber mihi est, 'I have a book'). Notice that the last one collides with the possessive genitive in spelling — the verb tells you which.",
